   ],
   "rule": {
    "title": "Endings straight onto the stem",
    "body": "Perfect middle/passive: reduplication + -μαι -σαι -ται -μεθα -σθε -νται with no connecting vowel: λέλυμαι, λέλυσαι, λέλυται. Consonant stems adjust the ending (γέγραπται). οἶδα (I know) is a perfect in form with present meaning.",
    "examples": [
     {
      "gr": "γέγραπται ἐν τῷ νόμῳ",
      "en": "it is written in the law"
     },
     {
      "gr": "σέσωσθε",
      "en": "you have been saved"
     },
     {
